	"note": "Per runtime key (Bun by minor, Node by major) and e2e build cell: the cell's build time over a honey-free reference build's (packages/core/tests/e2e/build-gate.ts), from the RATIO build lines of the build and prod e2e jobs of CI runs 40889301648, 40891096140, 40893983504, 40908742095, 40911060071, 40913885826 (ci.yml dispatched with build_mode=record). Each job is classed fast, middle or slow by its own surface builds on bun, Node-only jobs unclassified; byClass is each class's median. baseline: the median of every job's ratio. ceiling: the worst plus a 10% margin (worst x 1.10). A ratio above its ceiling is REGRESSED. catches: ceiling / baseline. No retry: a red with honey unchanged is answered by a re-record (6+ runs spanning both runner classes, derived by derive-build-ceilings.ts), never a rerun. Each cell's ratio is the median of k=3 app builds over the median of 5 reference builds (1a41b73); the hang guard judges every build. Ceilings judge only on GitHub Actions (GITHUB_ACTIONS=true, bd13cba); elsewhere they print report-only, since a local reference builds ~80 ms against CI's 140-230. Derived plain (all six pooled): --by-commit refused 25 cells as n=3 per commit, but 30ed81e..530b637 changes nothing the e2e builds bundle (packages/core only lint/spawners.js; packages/gen's Java emitter and runtime, tests, and the CLI's option parser), and the two groups' runner mixes differ (30ed81e all slow, 530b637 one fast and five slow). Speed check (H1): over the 18 classed Bun jobs, raw surface time rises 64% fast to slow while the ratio rises 7%; byClass fast rests on 2 jobs. History: k=1 ceilings from 11 runs (425f0a4) went red once on a single slow build with honey unchanged (40877110861, defaults x cloudflare 21.21 over 20.98); report-only from 16ea742 for this re-record; re-enforced here.",
